@startuml
!include _style.puml

title Perturbation: what one record turns into

start
:One SourceRecord\nlocal_id, name, system, country;
:Open this record's generator\nRandom(hash of run seed + local_id);

partition "Which scenarios apply" {
  while (Another scenario in the profile?) is (yes)
    :Take the scenario's own exclusions\nif it has a block, otherwise the\nprofile's (replaces, never merges);
    if (System excluded, country excluded,\nor any step's family excluded?) then (yes)
      :Not applicable to this record;
    else (no)
      :Applicable;
    endif
  endwhile
}

:Draw one value from the generator;

if (Any applicable scenario\nwith weight above zero?) then (no)
  :Row emitted unchanged\nscenario_id null,\nno steps reported;
  stop
else (yes)
  :Pick one scenario,\nweighted among those applicable;
endif

partition "Run that scenario's chain, in order" {
  while (Another step in the chain?) is (yes)
    :Find the operator's sites\nin the name as it stands now;
    :Trials = min(attempts, sites found);
    while (Another trial?) is (yes)
      :Draw twice: whether it fires,\nand which site;
      if (Fired?) then (yes)
        :Take that site, and discard\nevery site overlapping it;
      else (no)
        :Nothing taken\n(the two draws are spent either way);
      endif
    endwhile
    :Apply the taken changes\nright to left, highest offset first;
    if (Asked for changes and landed none?) then (yes)
      :Report this step in\nsteps_that_landed_nothing;
    else (no)
      :Record what landed\nas AppliedChange entries;
    endif
  endwhile
}

:Row emitted\nmutated name, original_name,\nscenario_id, changed;
stop

note right
  **One record in, exactly one row out**, whether or not
  anything landed. That is what keeps the perturbed set
  joinable one-to-one against its source.

  Nothing is drawn from entropy. One generator runs the
  whole chain and every trial spends the same two values
  whether it fires or not, so a step that lands nothing
  and a step that lands several leave the stream in the
  same place.
end note

@enduml
